spawnWait: run a program by argument vector, without /bin/sh (unix)

R's system() and system2() on unix start every program through
/bin/sh -c. R CMD INSTALL now starts `rzig build` (patch 0013), which
must work where no shell is installed: .Internal(spawnWait(argv,
timeout)) runs argv[0] (PATH lookup for a bare name) with the given
arguments through R's existing fork-and-wait machinery
(R_system_timeout's, with its timeout, signal handling and process
group), execvp in place of execl("/bin/sh", "-c", ...). The status is
system()'s: the exit code, 127 when the program cannot start, 124 after
the timeout. Windows' system2() already spawns without a shell (run.c),
so there it is not defined. feat-no-host-paths PLAN.md, S1;
feat-zig-pkg-build PLAN.md, milestone 3.

--- a/src/unix/sys-unix.c
+++ b/src/unix/sys-unix.c
@@ -638,12 +638,12 @@
